{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00838",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.62,
      "end_seconds": 13.89,
      "duration_seconds": 13.27,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I'm here, I suppose, because the district nurse said I should be. I'm fine. I'm just tired, and I'm sure it's nothing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.73,
      "end_seconds": 24.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "Thank you for coming, Mrs Dixon. Tell me a bit about your situation at home. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.6,
      "end_seconds": 40.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.74,
      "text": "My husband has dementia. He's been unwell for five years, and it's got worse this past year. I look after him full time. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.56,
      "end_seconds": 46.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "That sounds exhausting. What does a day look like? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.67,
      "end_seconds": 67.27,
      "duration_seconds": 18.6,
      "text": "Up at six to wash him, dress him, give him breakfast, and then I watch him all day. He wanders. I sleep in short bits, on the settee, in case he goes out. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.51,
      "end_seconds": 75.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "How long since you had a proper night's sleep? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.9,
      "end_seconds": 79.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Oh, months. I don't remember. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.86,
      "end_seconds": 89.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "How's your own health, how are you feeling in yourself? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.62,
      "end_seconds": 97.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Run down. A bit achy. I haven't had time to think about it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.68,
      "end_seconds": 105.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Any low mood, or feeling like you can't cope?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.37,
      "end_seconds": 111.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "No. I'm not depressed. No, I just get on with it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.49,
      "end_seconds": 116.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Any other health conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.55,
      "end_seconds": 122.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "High blood pressure, and I had a hysterectomy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.26,
      "end_seconds": 126.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "When was the hysterectomy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.93,
      "end_seconds": 130.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Twenty years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.93,
      "end_seconds": 133.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.48,
      "end_seconds": 141.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "My blood pressure tablet, amlodipine, 5 mg once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.82,
      "end_seconds": 147.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Who helps you at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.76,
      "end_seconds": 158.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Our daughter comes on Sundays. And the carers, for half an hour in the morning. That's all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.67,
      "end_seconds": 164.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Let me check your pulse and pressure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.79,
      "end_seconds": 167.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Go on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.53,
      "end_seconds": 188.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Pulse 78, blood pressure 144 over 86, weight 61 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.83,
      "end_seconds": 192.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Is that bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.94,
      "end_seconds": 205.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "Your pressure is a bit up, which is understandable with stress and little sleep. I'll listen to your chest. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.1,
      "end_seconds": 222.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.88,
      "end_seconds": 229.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Your chest is clear, and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.47,
      "end_seconds": 233.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.91,
      "end_seconds": 250.56,
      "duration_seconds": 14.65,
      "text": "Mrs Dixon, you're doing an enormous job, and you've not had time to look after yourself. I'm not worried about anything physical today, but I'm worried about you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.11,
      "end_seconds": 256.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I'm all right, really. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.11,
      "end_seconds": 268.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.26,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a blood test, to check your blood count, thyroid and vitamin D, as tiredness can have physical causes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.58,
      "end_seconds": 272.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.84,
      "end_seconds": 284.33,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "And I'd like to arrange a carer's assessment, so the council can offer you respite care, and some days off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.12,
      "end_seconds": 287.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "I couldn't leave him. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.77,
      "end_seconds": 299.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "Respite is a rest, so you can keep going. And there's a carers' support group, and a helpline."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.52,
      "end_seconds": 303.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I've seen the leaflet. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.26,
      "end_seconds": 317.81,
      "duration_seconds": 11.55,
      "text": "Please use it. If you ever feel you can't cope, feel low or hopeless, ring me straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.32,
      "end_seconds": 325.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. It's nice to be asked. ~"
    }
  ]
}
